    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Verify by direct expansion, and by taking out the common factor, that:\n$$(1+x)^4-(1+x)^3=x(1+x)^3$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both methods give $x(1+x)^3$.",
      "worked": "Method 1: Taking out common factor\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+x)^4-(1+x)^3&=(1+x)^3((1+x)-1)\\\\&=(1+x)^3(x)\\\\&=x(1+x)^3\\end{align*}$$\nMethod 2: Direct expansion\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+x)^4&=1+4x+6x^2+4x^3+x^4\\\\(1+x)^3&=1+3x+3x^2+x^3\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}(1+x)^4-(1+x)^3&=x+3x^2+3x^3+x^4\\\\&=x(1+3x+3x^2+x^3)\\\\&=x(1+x)^3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
